<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Davit Bek</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1728">1728</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Davit <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bek">Bek</a> was an Armenian military leader who led a revolt in Syunik, in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, from 1722, first against Persian khans and then against Ottoman invaders, as Safavid power collapsed. Backed by local meliks and in contact with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, he won several victories, notably at Halidzor in 1727. He died in 1728.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/davit-bek.jpg" alt="Davit Bek" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: harutune · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Davit_Bek_statue_Kapan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
